From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] a call of a proxied function the host library lacks returns 0 (and the names are logged) instead of aborting the process

proxy_library_builder.cc gives a known function with no host symbol (dlsym of the host library fails) the thunk DoBadThunk, which was LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL. Mesa
has no glCopyTextureCHROMIUM, glCopySubTexture3DANGLE, glProvokingVertexANGLE and the like, but the guest libGLESv2 proxy exports them as Android's does, so Gecko's
GL loader (eglGetProcAddress fails, then dlsym of the library) got non-NULL pointers and calling one aborted Fennec's GPU process ("Bad thunk call before ..."
in its component log, right after the five "eglGetProcAddress(...) failed" lines). The parent's main thread then waited for ever for that process's sync IPC reply
(MOZ_LOG ipc: "Send seqno=-29, xid=-29", never answered): no page request, no beacon. DoBadThunk now logs the call site and returns 0 (what a driver without
the function gives a caller that ignores a missing extension); InterceptSymbol logs every name that gets it. Regression: tests/apps/hello-arm64 (missingGlFunctions).
Module libberberis_arm64.

